{"a1":[{"k":"title","cap":"Days Until a Warmer Day","say":"Let's solve Days Until a Warmer Day, using the Monotonic Stack approach.","card":{"title":"Days Until a Warmer Day","sub":"Monotonic Stack · Medium","pattern":"monotonic-stack"}},{"k":"problem","cap":"temps[i] is the temperature on day i. For each day, return how many days you must wait for a strictly warmer temperature, or 0 if no warmer day comes.","say":"temps at i is the temperature on day i. For each day, return how many days you must wait for a strictly warmer temperature, or 0 if no warmer day comes.","card":{"lines":["temps[i] is the temperature on day i. For each day, return how many days you must wait for a strictly warmer temperature, or 0 if no warmer day comes."]}},{"k":"example","cap":"For example, with temps = [73,74,75,71,69,72,76,73], the answer is [1,1,4,2,1,1,0,0].","say":"For example, with temps equals 73, 74, 75, 71, 69, 72, 76, 73, the answer is 1, 1, 4, 2, 1, 1, 0, 0.","card":{"lines":["Input: temps = [73,74,75,71,69,72,76,73]","Output: [1,1,4,2,1,1,0,0]"]}},{"k":"idea","cap":"Keep a stack of days still waiting for a warmer day; their temperatures decrease from bottom to top.","card":{"pattern":"monotonic-stack","name":"Monotonic Stack"}},{"k":"idea","cap":"Each new day pops every waiting day that is colder, because today is their answer. Then today joins the stack and waits.","card":{"pattern":"monotonic-stack","name":"Monotonic Stack"}},{"k":"trace","cap":"Let's walk through it with temps = [73,74,75,71,69,72,76].","say":"Let's walk through it with temps equals 73, 74, 75, 71, 69, 72, 76.","st":{"arrays":[{"n":"temps","v":["73","74","75","71","69","72","76"],"p":[{"l":"today","i":0}]}],"stacks":[{"n":"waiting days","v":["0"],"t":"stack"}],"out":{"n":"res","v":["0","0","0","0","0","0","0"]}}},{"k":"step","cap":"Day 0 (73°) starts waiting.","say":"Day 0 (73 degrees ) starts waiting.","ln":{"python":7,"java":10},"st":{"arrays":[{"n":"temps","v":["73","74","75","71","69","72","76"],"p":[